# `since` also marks time and `as` also marks manner or comparison, so
# a reader has to pick the reading. `because` marks only a cause.
#
# After a comma, `since` before a determiner, pronoun, or proper noun
# marked a cause in 13 of 14 sampled hits (`, since the lock is
# held`). A temporal `since` after a comma (`, since the upgrade
# landed`) still fires.
#
# Without a comma, `since` counts when a present-tense auxiliary follows
# its subject, directly or after one word (`since the lock is held`,
# `Since this is rarely needed`). A temporal `since` names a past event
# (`since the upgrade landed`) or a version (`Since v2.3, the flag
# ...`), so it has no such auxiliary and passes. All 24 hits of this
# shape in the kubernetes and nix.dev docs marked a cause. The filter
# narrows the finding to `since`. `needs` and `will` stay out of the
# auxiliary list, because the obligation, no-negation, and future-tense
# rules report the words after them.
#
# `as` counts only before a subject pronoun and a finite verb (`, as
# it is deprecated`). `you` and `we` stay out, because `as you can
# see` and `as we have seen` are the filler ProseFiller reports. `do`
# and `does` stay out, because `, as it does for any key` compares.
expr subject [it, they, this, these, there]
expr verb [is, are, was, were, has, have, can, will]
expr aux [is, are, has, have, can, cannot, does, do]
expr main [((,) [(since [DET, PRON, PROPN]), (as @subject @verb)]), <(since [DET, PRON, PROPN] @aux), since>, <(since [DET, PRON, PROPN] * @aux), since>]
let message "Causal since or as. Write because."
let description "Flags since and as where they mark a cause, which because marks in one reading."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
let scope "Sentence"
allows "Since v2.3, the flag defaults to true."
allows "The hook skips the key, as it does for any unknown key."
allows "The job runs as root."
